 "_about": "Public-domain Ashton Oxenden (1808-1892), rector of Pluckley and Bishop of Montreal, for the Word Hoard: his plain devotional and teaching books, among them The Pathway of Safety (first called Counsel to the Awakened), Fervent Prayer, Baptism Simply Explained, The Lord's Supper Simply Explained, Cottage Sermons, The Parables of Our Lord, A Simple Exposition of the Psalms, The Earnest Communicant, Touchstones, My First Year in Canada and The History of My Life (1891). Texts are from Internet Archive scans. Added 2026-10-23 by lane A, round 74 (my pick); Adam may veto the whole shelf. Every printing dated before 1930, so public domain in the US. No uids minted.",
